-- Migration: state sources, week 2 (docs/SOURCE_REGISTRY.md §7). Data only, additive.
-- 1. The Illinois, North Carolina and Utah feed connectors (lib/grants/states), registered DISABLED:
--    none of their terms could be confirmed as permitting automated reading on 7 Nov 2026,
--    and the daily grant sync runs a state feed only while its row is active with checked terms.
-- 2. Watch lists for the ten most populous states not already covered by a feed
--    (CA has an active feed; IL and NC have feeds above): official .gov pages that list
--    funding opportunities, registered DISABLED until a person checks each site's terms.
-- Nothing here publishes an opportunity. ON CONFLICT keeps any row a person already edited.
INSERT INTO "grant_sources" ("id", "key", "name", "jurisdiction_kind", "jurisdiction_code", "connector_type", "connector", "urls", "schedule_hours", "owner", "status", "terms_note", "terms_checked", "terms_permit_automation")
VALUES
  ('src-il-csfa', 'il_csfa', 'Illinois CSFA opportunity list', 'state', 'IL', 'feed', 'il_csfa', '["https://omb.illinois.gov/public/gata/csfa/OpportunityList.aspx"]'::jsonb, 24, 'ebyron357', 'disabled',
   'Not confirmed (7 Nov 2026). Read: State of Illinois Privacy Notice, Legal Notices (https://www.illinois.gov/about/privacy.html): "Access to the State of Illinois websites is provided subject to the following terms and conditions"; use is at the user''s sole risk and must conform to applicable laws; links are not endorsements. It says nothing about automated reading and does not name omb.illinois.gov. No terms page for omb.illinois.gov was found. https://omb.illinois.gov/robots.txt redirects to an access gateway page reading "Unauthorized access is prohibited. Further access is limited to authorized users only." The opportunity list itself is public, with no sign-in. A person must confirm with Illinois OMB (GATA) that automated reading of the list is permitted before enabling.',
   false, false),
  ('src-nc-grant-directory', 'nc_grant_directory', 'NC.gov grant opportunities directory', 'state', 'NC', 'feed', 'nc_grant_directory', '["https://www.nc.gov/your-government/all-nc-state-services/grant-opportunities"]'::jsonb, 24, 'ebyron357', 'disabled',
   'Not permitted for this product as read (7 Nov 2026). Read: NC.gov Disclaimer & Terms of Use (https://www.nc.gov/disclaimer-terms-use, last updated 7 Nov 2025): State websites "shall only be used for general informational purposes"; "Unless otherwise noted on an individual document, the State of North Carolina grants permission to copy and distribute non-image files, documents, and information for non-commercial use, provided they are copied and distributed without alteration and appropriately cite to the source"; use of photos and images is prohibited. GrantCrest is a paid product, so that permission does not cover it. Also read: NC.gov Privacy Policy (https://nc.gov/privacy): "you should request explicit permission before reproducing or distributing any content"; https://www.nc.gov/robots.txt: "User-agent: * Allow: /". Ask NC DIT for written permission for commercial use before enabling. Even when enabled, directory rows are "listed", never published: the directory states no deadlines.',
   false, false),
  ('src-ut-funding-portal', 'ut_funding_portal', 'Utah Funding Opportunities Portal', 'state', 'UT', 'feed', 'ut_funding_portal', '["https://lookerstudio.google.com/u/0/reporting/ef90555b-7a4d-4b8e-898e-c427c996bf65/page/WFAzC"]'::jsonb, 24, 'ebyron357', 'disabled',
   'Not confirmed (7 Nov 2026). The listing is a Google Looker Studio report linked from the Governor''s Office of Planning and Budget Funding Resources page (https://gopb.utah.gov/funding-resources/), which states no terms of use. Reading it needs a browser through two cross-origin iframes; the API server has none, so the connector cannot run here even if enabled. Access goes through Google''s Terms of Service (https://policies.google.com/terms), which the fetch tool could not open. Ask GOPB for an export, or for permission, before enabling. Even when enabled, rows are "listed", never published: the cards state no deadlines.',
   false, false),
  ('src-tx-egrants', 'tx_egrants_funding_opportunities', 'Texas eGrants funding opportunities (Office of the Governor)', 'state', 'TX', 'portal_page', NULL, '["https://egrants.gov.texas.gov/apps/egrants/fundopp.aspx"]'::jsonb, 24, 'ebyron357', 'disabled',
   'Terms not checked. Page read 7 Nov 2026: the Office of the Governor eGrants funding announcement list (titles and due dates; many rows were past due; details open through JavaScript postbacks). The page links to no terms of use. Read the Office of the Governor site policies before enabling.',
   false, false),
  ('src-fl-dep-grants', 'fl_dep_protecting_florida_together_grants', 'Florida DEP grants (Protecting Florida Together)', 'state', 'FL', 'watched_page', NULL, '["https://protectingfloridatogether.gov/Grants"]'::jsonb, 24, 'ebyron357', 'disabled',
   'Terms not checked. Page read 7 Nov 2026: the Florida Department of Environmental Protection grants portal; it links to category pages (water quality, land and recreation, resilience) that list open opportunities, and lists none itself. No statewide Florida list of open State grants was found. Read before enabling: https://floridadep.gov/disclaimer#ProtectingFloridaTogether and https://floridadep.gov/privacy-statement.',
   false, false),
  ('src-ny-sfs-funding-search', 'ny_sfs_funding_search', 'New York Statewide Financial System funding search', 'state', 'NY', 'portal_page', NULL, '["https://esupplier.sfs.ny.gov/psp/fscm/SUPPLIER/ERP/c/NY_SUPPUB_FL.AUC_RESP_INQ_AUC.GBL"]'::jsonb, 24, 'ebyron357', 'disabled',
   'Terms not checked. Not read directly: the address is the public SFS opportunity search linked from https://grantsmanagement.ny.gov/search-funding-sfs (read 7 Nov 2026), which says opportunities can be viewed without a user name. It is a PeopleSoft application that needs JavaScript, so the built-in fetcher will likely read no listings; changedetection.io''s browser fetcher may. Read before enabling: https://grantsmanagement.ny.gov/website-disclaimer and https://grantsmanagement.ny.gov/privacy-policy.',
   false, false),
  ('src-ny-dos-funding', 'ny_dos_funding_opportunities', 'New York Department of State funding opportunities', 'state', 'NY', 'watched_page', NULL, '["https://dos.ny.gov/funding-bid-opportunities"]'::jsonb, 24, 'ebyron357', 'disabled',
   'Terms not checked. Page read 7 Nov 2026: lists current Department of State requests for applications (for example the 2026-2027 Smart Growth Community Planning Grant Program); dates are in each entry''s schedule section. Read before enabling: https://dos.ny.gov/disclaimer and https://dos.ny.gov/privacy-policy.',
   false, false),
  ('src-ny-agm-funding', 'ny_agm_funding_opportunities', 'New York Agriculture and Markets funding opportunities', 'state', 'NY', 'watched_page', NULL, '["https://agriculture.ny.gov/funding-opportunities"]'::jsonb, 24, 'ebyron357', 'disabled',
   'Terms not checked. Page read 7 Nov 2026: lists current requests for proposals and applications with due dates (for example RFP 0430, Climate Resilient Farming Program, Round 10). Read before enabling: https://agriculture.ny.gov/disclaimer and https://agriculture.ny.gov/privacy-policy.',
   false, false),
  ('src-pa-grants', 'pa_grants', 'Pennsylvania state grants (pa.gov/grants)', 'state', 'PA', 'portal_page', NULL, '["https://pa.gov/en/grants"]'::jsonb, 24, 'ebyron357', 'disabled',
   'Terms not checked. Page read 7 Nov 2026: the Commonwealth''s grant search, which says it "features funding opportunities from more than 20 agencies"; listings are on its search page and may load with JavaScript. Read before enabling: https://www.pa.gov/privacy-policy (Privacy and Disclaimers) and https://www.pa.gov/security-policy.',
   false, false),
  ('src-oh-grants-partnership', 'oh_grants_partnership_funding_opportunities', 'Ohio Grants Partnership funding opportunities', 'state', 'OH', 'portal_page', NULL, '["https://www.grants.ohio.gov/fundingopportunities.aspx"]'::jsonb, 24, 'ebyron357', 'disabled',
   'Terms not checked, and the page was not read: the fetch tool could not open it on 7 Nov 2026. The address is the statewide list of active funding opportunities that the Ohio Department of Education and Workforce links from https://education.ohio.gov/Topics/Finance-and-Funding/Grants-Administration/Grant-Opportunities. Confirm the page and its site terms before enabling.',
   false, false),
  ('src-ga-opb-grants', 'ga_opb_grant_opportunities', 'Georgia Governor''s Office of Planning and Budget grant opportunities', 'state', 'GA', 'portal_page', NULL, '["https://opb.georgia.gov/node/13841"]'::jsonb, 24, 'ebyron357', 'disabled',
   'Terms not checked. Page read 7 Nov 2026: titled "Grant Opportunities", it said "There are currently no active grant opportunities available." No statewide Georgia list of open State grants was found. Read before enabling: https://georgia.gov/privacysecurity.',
   false, false),
  ('src-mi-mde-grants', 'mi_mde_grants', 'Michigan Department of Education grants', 'state', 'MI', 'watched_page', NULL, '["https://michigan.gov/mde/Services/financial-management/grants"]'::jsonb, 24, 'ebyron357', 'disabled',
   'Terms not checked. Page read 7 Nov 2026: lists federal and state grants the department manages with application windows (for example Robotics Completion Grant, Section 99h, 10/19/2026 to 12/01/2026). No statewide Michigan list of open State grants was found. Read before enabling: https://www.michigan.gov/policies.',
   false, false)
